   "source": {
    "label": "thrm:dal_reg",
    "number": "Theorem 4.8",
    "quote": "For the PS setting, consider DAL with a detector $\\mathcal{D}$ that satisfies Property \\ref{proper:good_CD}, a stationary bandit algorithm $\\mathcal{B}$ with regret upper bound $R_{\\mathcal{B}}$ concave and increasing with $T$ ... If Assumption \\ref{assum:cp_assum} holds, $\\alpha_{k} =\\sqrt{k|\\mathcal{C}|N_{\\mathrm{e}}}/(2\\sqrt{T}\\log^2 T)$, $\\delta_{\\mathrm{F}}=\\delta_{\\mathrm{D}}=T^{-\\eta}$ ... then DAL's regret satisfies $R_T = \\tilde{\\mathcal{O}} (d^p \\gamma_T^q (|\\mathcal{A}|\\log|\\Pi|)^{r} \\sqrt{N_{T} T} + \\sqrt{|\\mathcal{C}|N_{\\mathrm{e}}N_{T}T})$."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
